KG42.register("clusters-9f4b26e61ab6bc1dc0820838",{"id":"44-blockchain_phev_trading::v142-d-K002","paper":"44-blockchain_phev_trading","label":"Execution of local electric energy trading and energy coin fulfillment settlement","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"Execution of local electric energy trading and energy coin fulfillment settlement","market_meaning":"PHEVs equipped with bidirectional charging equipment trade electric energy locally, and the LAG trading server coordinates charging-pile switches to complete energy delivery; after the transaction, the buyer pays energy coins through a wallet address based on metering records. The existing auction payment and reward functions are retained as amount rules; a party that suddenly disconnects during a planned transaction bears the penalty obligation described in the original chain.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M01"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["activation","settlement","pricing"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The product, switch execution, and post-transaction payment belong to local PHEV trading of the same mechanism. Bidirectional charging capability, transaction completion, and planned-transaction disconnection each qualify their respective clauses. R008 shares only its alternative expression of payment rewards, and the theorem statement is not turned into a precondition for energy delivery or wallet payment; the correspondence from payment rewards to metered quantity, wallet transfer, and energy-coin amount remains unresolved.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The boundary is constituted by the actual transaction, the metering basis, and post-transaction wallet fulfillment, and the source explicitly supports the functional link between execution and payment. The shared pricing formula is used to avoid double-counting monetary rules; this cluster does not reconstruct the auction algorithm and does not insert blockchain audit responsibilities into the local coordination node. The lack of interfaces among amounts, metering, and transfer means that the fulfillment rules are not yet closed.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides the local energy-delivery execution responsibility, charging-pile switch control, and bidirectional-equipment trading capability."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R009","ownership":"primary","role":"support","rationale":"Clarifies the local electric-energy product and buyer and seller roles corresponding to execution and settlement, and retains the bidirectional charging equipment condition."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R010","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provides post-transaction payment according to metering, wallet energy-coin transfer, payment-reward amount rules, and the penalty obligation for disconnection during a planned transaction."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R008","ownership":"shared","role":"alternative","rationale":"Only equations (15) and (16) together with their bids and parameters are shared as an alternative expression of the R010 amount rules; their primary attribution to auction pricing and the welfare theorem remains in v142-d-K001, and they are not counted as a separate rule."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R009","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R009::phi::v141-c-R009-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e016","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g03-E03"],"rationale":"The local electric-energy product, the buy-sell roles for charging and discharging, and the bidirectional charging equipment condition in the source match the same kind of physical transaction coordinated by the LAG; this is a complementarity between product scope and execution responsibility, and no equipment or product dependency edge is added."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::E::v141-c-R010-E002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e016","v141-b-g01-e044"],"rationale":"The source associates actual energy delivery, real-time metering, and post-transaction wallet payment with the same energy transaction; R010 already has a frozen edge in which the transaction precedes payment, and here only the cross-chain execution and fulfillment semantics are connected."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R008","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R010","kind":"alternative_representation","from_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The two chains preserve the same (15) and (16) from the pricing and settlement perspectives respectively; the amount rules are accessed only as two expressions of the same object, are not counted as an additional independent rule, and it is not asserted from this that pairwise wallet transfer amounts have been defined."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R010::V::coordination.local_operator"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R008::V::coordination.local_operator","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e015","v141-b-g01-e020","v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E10"],"rationale":"Both reference the same existing LAG coordination function node, involving execution, auction transfer rules, and settlement responsibilities respectively; this is not taken to mean that it carries blockchain audit functions."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","v141-c-R010::V::execution.energy_trade"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R005::V::execution.energy_trade","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e016","v141-b-g01-e044"],"rationale":"One reference describes energy-delivery execution, and the other describes that transaction function before payment; the function node display is unified, and all original relationships are retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M03","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_b_ij_n","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E09","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The same buyer bilateral bid appears in payment pricing and in the settlement amount rules; its local variable definition is retained, and the bid is not directly treated as metered electric quantity or as a pairwise transfer amount."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M04","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::x::x_s_ji_n","v141-c-R010::x::v141-c-R010-X002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E08","v141-b-g02-E10","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The same seller bilateral bid enters the same reward function in both chains; the local roles and original domains remain separate."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M05","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_l1","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"The source explicitly identifies it as the same cost factor and uses it in the same reward rule; one unspecified value and the other description of a positive sign value are retained, and no unified parameter is rewritten."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M06","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::theta::theta_rmin_j","v141-c-R010::theta::v141-c-R010-T002"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E23"],"rationale":"Both are the same participation-reward term; the local unit expressions in USD and in US dollars in the numerical study are retained as they are, and their exchange relationship with energy coins is not presumed."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M07","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C002","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"Both fully express the same charging-PHEV payment function (15), with the same applicable objects and summation scope; the settlement expression is chosen as the display representative, while the pricing expression and its binding remain accessible."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M08","kind":"same_expression","member_refs":["v141-c-R008::phi::v141-c-R008-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E14"],"rationale":"Both fully express the same discharging-PHEV reward function (16), including the same cost factor and minimum participation reward; only display duplication is eliminated, and neither original object is deleted."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"The sources for execution, metering, energy-coin payment, and amount functions all remain unverified; the shared-formula mapping is also only a candidate interpretation permitted by the experiment.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R009","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e001","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e016","v141-b-g01-e044","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g03-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"In subsequent work, independently check the sources, formula consistency, and the applicable scope of the same transaction; this round does not claim that source audit or scientific confirmation has been completed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"C does not give the interface from the clearing plan to actual metered delivery, nor does it explain how the buyer's total payment and the seller's total reward calculated from bids correspond to metering records, pairwise wallet transfers, auctioneer retention, and the energy-coin amount. The US-dollar basis of the numerical study cannot be directly taken as the energy-coin denomination.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010","v141-c-R008"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C005","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C006","v141-c-R008::theta::theta_rmin_j"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e008","v141-b-g01-e009","v141-b-g01-e016","v141-b-g01-e017","v141-b-g01-e044","v141-b-g02-E14","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E24"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Supplement the source-supported mappings among plan, delivery, metering, and monetary amounts, and clarify pairwise allocation, fee retention, and the energy-coin pricing or exchange basis; if the source does not define them, continue to retain the gap."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The statement that no trusted third party for transactions is needed has not been expanded in existing C into payment verification, transaction-record signing, authorized LAG audit, and consensus acceptance conditions. The related node proposals are still pending, and these functions cannot be assumed by default to be existing semantics of the local coordination or physical execution node.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R005","v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C003","v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C004","v141-c-R010::V::settlement.payment"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e012","v141-b-g01-e013","v141-b-g01-e037","v141-b-g01-e038","v141-b-g01-e045","v141-b-g01-e046","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g03-E04"],"proposal_ids":["v141-b-g01-p001","proposal:v141-b-g02-blockchain-audit","v141-b-g03-P01"],"required_work":"A human is to check the overlap and applicable scope of these pending proposals, and then upstream is to form a referenceable verification rule chain; this round does not insert new nodes and does not claim that consensus or payment-finality conditions have been closed."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R010 retains the penalty obligation for a party that suddenly disconnects during a planned transaction, but there is no penalty amount, calculation method, receiving entity, or enforcement determination; this obligation cannot be generalized to all abnormal events or all PHEV departures.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R010"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R010::phi::v141-c-R010-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E20"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the planned time period, the determination of disconnection responsibility, and the available sources for the penalty; when quantitative provisions are lacking, retain the qualitative obligation and do not generate a computable penalty rule."}]},"rule_refs":["44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R005","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R009","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R010","44-blockchain_phev_trading::v141-c-R008"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-0af19b0c67c825ec","COMP-230dbf46f02b4bfe","COMP-6b2172d51d331629","COMP-93c52ad833d04287","KG40-404d7eddbf0fc37c"]});
